('event.mexica.quetzalcoatl_tollan_end','End of Quetzalcoatl''s glory at Tollan','羽蛇神在图拉的衰落',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.mexica',NULL,'Florentine Codex Book 3, chapters 3–14: sorcerers including Titlacauan come to Quetzalcoatl and his glory at Tollan ends.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('site.mexico.templo_mayor','Templo Mayor of Tenochtitlan','特诺奇蒂特兰大神庙','Huey Teocalli',NULL,'TEMPLE','civ.mexica',NULL,'Twin-shrine pyramid of Tenochtitlan with a southern chapel of Huitzilopochtli and a northern temple of Tlaloc, as described by INAH.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('monument.maya.el_castillo_chichen','El Castillo (Temple of Kukulkan), Chichen-Itza','奇琴伊察卡斯蒂略（库库尔坎神庙）','El Castillo',NULL,'MONUMENT','civ.maya',NULL,'Principal monument of the northern group at Chichen-Itza, also known as the Temple of Kukulkan (UNESCO 483).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('museum.maya.chahk_plate_met','Plate with the god Chahk (Met 2021.320)','大都会博物馆恰克神陶盘',NULL,NULL,'MUSEUM_OBJECT','civ.maya',NULL,'Classic Maya codex-style footed plate showing the rain god Chahk waist-deep in watery motifs.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('place.sumerian.dilmun','Dilmun (in Enki and Ninhursaĝa)','迪尔蒙（《恩基与宁胡尔萨格》）','Dilmun',NULL,'MYTHICAL_PLACE','civ.sumerian',NULL,'The pure land where Enki and Ninhursaĝa''s story begins; the historical Dilmun is not inferred from this narrative.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.sumerian.enki_ninhursag','Enki''s illness and Ninhursaĝa''s healing','恩基的病与宁胡尔萨格的救治',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.sumerian',NULL,'In ETCSL 1.1.1 Enki eats the plants, Ninhursaĝa curses him, and later she brings forth deities to heal his ailing body.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.sumerian.nanna_journey','Nanna-Suen''s journey to Nibru','南纳前往尼普尔的旅程',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.sumerian',NULL,'The moon god travels by boat with gifts to his father Enlil''s city Nibru and returns with blessings for Urim.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('hero.sumerian.gilgamesh','Gilgameš (Sumerian poems)','吉尔伽美什（苏美尔语诗篇）','Bilgames',NULL,'HERO','civ.sumerian',NULL,'Lord of Unug (Uruk) in the Sumerian Gilgameš poems; kept separate from the later Akkadian epic''s text entity.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('monster.sumerian.huwawa','Ḫuwawa','胡瓦瓦','Ḫuwawa',NULL,'MONSTER','civ.sumerian',NULL,'Guardian of the mountains of cedar confronted by Gilgameš in ETCSL 1.8.1.5.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.sumerian.gilgamesh_huwawa','Gilgameš''s expedition against Ḫuwawa','吉尔伽美什远征胡瓦瓦',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.sumerian',NULL,'Gilgameš sets out for the mountains; Utu is asked for help and grants guides.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('concept.chinese.bagua','Eight Trigrams (bagua)','八卦','八卦','bāguà','CONCEPT','civ.chinese_ancient',NULL,'The eight three-line figures that the Xi Ci II says Baoxi (Fuxi) first made after observing heaven, earth and living things.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('text.chinese.zhouyi_xici','Xi Ci commentary of the Zhouyi','《周易·系辞》','繫辭','Xì cí','TEXT','civ.chinese_ancient','Received Warring States–Han layer; dating debated','One of the Ten Wings of the Zhouyi; part 2 lists the inventions of the ancient sages beginning with Baoxi.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.chinese.fuxi_makes_trigrams','Fuxi makes the eight trigrams','伏羲始作八卦',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.chinese_ancient',NULL,'Xi Ci II: Baoxi looks up to heaven and down to earth, observes birds, beasts and the land, and first makes the eight trigrams.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('hero.chinese.chiyou','Chiyou','蚩尤','蚩尤','Chīyóu','HERO','civ.chinese_ancient','Received early Chinese narrative layers','Rebellious lord who, in the Shiji Annals of the Five Emperors, disobeys the ruler and is captured and killed by Xuanyuan at Zhuolu.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"reality": "LEGENDARY_FIGURE"}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.chinese.battle_of_zhuolu','Battle in the wilds of Zhuolu','涿鹿之战',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.chinese_ancient',NULL,'Shiji, Annals of the Five Emperors: Xuanyuan gathers the lords'' troops, fights Chiyou in the wilds of Zhuolu, and captures and kills him.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('text.chinese.sanwu_liji','Sanwu liji (lost; known from quotations)','《三五历纪》','三五曆紀','Sān wǔ lì jì','TEXT','civ.chinese_ancient','Three Kingdoms (3rd century CE), attributed','Lost work attributed to Xu Zheng of the Three Kingdoms state of Wu; its Pangu passage survives through quotations in later encyclopedias.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.chinese.pangu_heaven_earth','Pangu between heaven and earth (Sanwu liji)','盘古开天地（《三五历纪》）',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.chinese_ancient',NULL,'As quoted from the Sanwu liji: heaven and earth separate from an egg-like chaos and grow apart for 18,000 years while Pangu grows between them.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.chinese.nezha_fights_wukong','Nezha fights Sun Wukong (Journey to the West ch. 4)','哪吒大战孙悟空（《西游记》第四回）',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Novel episode: sent with Heavenly King Li against the self-styled Great Sage, Nezha takes three heads and six arms and is driven off by Sun Wukong.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('text.irish.cath_maige_tuired','Cath Maige Tuired (The Second Battle of Mag Tuired)','《第二次马格图雷德之战》','Cath Maige Tuired',NULL,'TEXT','civ.irish','Medieval Irish saga (manuscript Harley 5280; composition dates debated)','Medieval Irish saga of the war between the Túatha Dé Danann and the Fomoire, edited and translated by Elizabeth A. Gray (1982).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.irish.second_battle_mag_tuired','Second Battle of Mag Tuired','第二次马格图雷德之战',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.irish',NULL,'Battle between the Túatha Dé Danann and the Fomoire in Cath Maige Tuired, in which Lug kills Balor.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('artifact.irish.dagda_cauldron','The Dagda''s cauldron','达格达的大锅',NULL,NULL,'SACRED_OBJECT','civ.irish',NULL,'One of the four treasures of the Túatha Dé Danann in Cath Maige Tuired §6: brought from Murias, no company ever left it unsatisfied.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('being.irish.balor','Balor','巴洛尔','Balor',NULL,'ENTITY','civ.irish',NULL,'Fomorian champion in Cath Maige Tuired whose destructive eye is opened only on the battlefield; Lug kills him with a sling stone.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"group": "Fomoire"}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.slavic.kyiv_idols_980','Volodimer''s idols on the Kyiv hill (980)','980 年基辅山岗神像',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.slavic',NULL,'Primary Chronicle annal 980: Volodimer sets up idols of Perun, Khors, Dazhbog, Stribog, Simargl and Mokosh on the hill outside the palace hall.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.slavic.idols_cast_down_988','The Kyiv idols are cast down (988)','988 年推倒基辅神像',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.slavic',NULL,'Primary Chronicle annal 988: after his baptism Volodimer orders the idols overthrown; Perun is dragged down the hill and thrown into the Dnieper.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('text.zoroastrian.mihr_yasht','Mihr Yasht (Yasht 10)','《密赫尔颂》（第十颂）','Miθra Yašt',NULL,'SCRIPTURE','civ.zoroastrian','Young Avestan; dating debated','Avestan hymn to Mithra, one of the longest Yashts; translated by Darmesteter in the Sacred Books of the East.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('text.zoroastrian.videvdad_fargard1','Videvdad, Fargard 1 (the sixteen lands)','《万迪达德》第一章（十六地）','Vīdēvdād 1',NULL,'SCRIPTURE','civ.zoroastrian','Young Avestan; dating debated','First chapter of the Videvdad: sixteen good lands made by Ahura Mazda, each answered by a counter-creation of Angra Mainyu.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('place.zoroastrian.airyana_vaejah','Airyana Vaejah','雅利安瓦伊贾','Airiiana Vaējah','Airyana Vaējah','MYTHICAL_PLACE','civ.zoroastrian',NULL,'First of the good lands made by Ahura Mazda in Videvdad 1, ''by the good river Daitya''; not mapped to coordinates.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.zoroastrian.sixteen_lands','Creation of the sixteen lands and their counter-creations','十六地的创造与反创造',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.zoroastrian',NULL,'Videvdad 1: Ahura Mazda makes sixteen good lands; each time Angra Mainyu counter-creates a plague.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('site.hawaii.halemaumau','Halemaʻumaʻu crater, Kīlauea','哈雷茂茂火山口','Halemaʻumaʻu',NULL,'PLACE','civ.hawaiian',NULL,'Crater at the summit of Kīlauea that NPS describes as Pele''s home in Hawaiian tradition; a sacred landscape.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.hawaiian.pele_journey','Pele''s journey from Kahiki','佩蕾从卡希基出发的旅程',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.hawaiian',NULL,'NPS summary of Hawaiian oral history: Pele voyages from Kahiki, moves southeast through the islands and settles in Halemaʻumaʻu.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('event.maori.separation_rangi_papa','Separation of Ranginui and Papatūānuku','兰吉努伊与帕帕图阿努库的分离',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.maori',NULL,'Common thread named by Te Ara: the children of Ranginui and Papatūānuku separate their parents, letting light into the world.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z'),
('site.nigeria.osun_osogbo','Osun-Osogbo Sacred Grove','奥孙-奥索博神树林',NULL,NULL,'PLACE','civ.yoruba',NULL,'Dense forest on the outskirts of Osogbo, inscribed on the World Heritage List in 2005; UNESCO regards it as the abode of the Yoruba goddess Osun.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z','2026-10-09T00:30:00Z');

