UPDATE entities SET description='与亚述城相关的神；联合国教科文组织称该城为亚述人的宗教首都。 / God associated with the city of Ashur, which UNESCO calls the religious capital of the Assyrians.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.assyrian.ashur' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《系辞下》中的包牺氏（伏羲）：仰观天象、俯察地法，始作八卦，又结绳为网。 / Baoxi (Fuxi) in Xi Ci II: the ancient ruler who observed heaven, earth and living things, first made the eight trigrams and knotted nets.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.chinese.fu_xi' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《西游记》第四回中托塔李天王的三太子，变三头六臂迎战孙悟空（后世文学层）。 / Third prince of Heavenly King Li in Journey to the West ch. 4, who takes three heads and six arms against Sun Wukong (later literary layer).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.chinese.nezha' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='胡狼头神；在大英博物馆《阿尼纸草》第3框的称量心脏场景中扶稳天平。 / Jackal-headed god who steadies the balance in the weighing of Ani''s heart (British Museum EA10470,3).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.anubis' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='大地之神；在 UCL 的综述中是舒与泰芙努特之子，与天空女神努特被分开。 / Earth god, child of Shu and Tefnet in the UCL synthesis, held apart from the sky goddess Nut.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.geb' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='在《天牛之书》中，拉的眼睛喝下红色啤酒后回归的慈爱、母性的形象。 / In the Tale of the Heavenly Cow, the loving, maternal character to which the raging Eye of Ra returns after drinking red beer.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.hathor' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='在 UCL 对奥西里斯故事的概述中，伊西斯收集奥西里斯的肢体并怀上荷鲁斯；大都会博物馆的哀悼像把她与奈芙蒂斯配成一对。 / In the UCL summary of the Osiris cycle Isis gathers Osiris''s limbs and conceives Horus; Met mourning figures pair her with Nephthys.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.isis' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='大都会博物馆托勒密时期木像中的哀悼女神，与伊西斯一起出现在奥西里斯遗体两侧。 / Mourning goddess shown kneeling in a Ptolemaic wooden figure at the Met, paired with Isis around the body of Osiris.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.nephthys' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='天空女神；在 UCL 的综述中是舒与泰芙努特之女，与大地之神盖布被分开。 / Sky goddess, child of Shu and Tefnet in the UCL synthesis, held apart from the earth god Geb.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.nut' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='意为“强大的女神”：《天牛之书》中拉的眼睛化成的毁灭形态，几乎灭绝人类。 / ''The mighty goddess'': the destructive form of Ra''s Eye that almost annihilates humankind in the Tale of the Heavenly Cow.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.sekhmet' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='在 UCL 对奥西里斯故事的概述中，是奥西里斯“无序的兄弟”，杀害奥西里斯并取代他为王。 / Anarchic brother of Osiris who murders him and takes his place as king, in the UCL summary of the Osiris cycle.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.seth' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='UCL 数字埃及：太阳神阿图姆的第一个男性“子嗣”，名字与“干燥”相关；盖布与努特之父，并把天地分开。 / UCL Digital Egypt: first male offshoot of the sun-god Atum, linked with dryness; father of Geb and Nut and the one who holds earth and sky apart.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.shu' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='UCL 数字埃及：阿图姆的第一个女性“子嗣”，被解读为“湿润”；盖布与努特之母。 / UCL Digital Egypt: first female offshoot of the sun-god Atum, read as moisture; mother of Geb and Nut.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.tefnut' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='在阿尼的心脏称量场景中出现两次：天平上的狒狒，以及手持调色板的朱鹭头“众神书吏”。 / Shown twice in the weighing of Ani''s heart: as a baboon on the balance and as the ibis-headed scribe of the gods.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.egyptian.thoth' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='夏威夷火山之神；据美国国家公园管理局对口述传统的概述，她从卡希基远航而来，定居基拉韦厄的哈雷茂茂火山口。 / Hawaiian volcano deity who, in NPS''s summary of oral history, voyaged from Kahiki and made her home in Halemaʻumaʻu crater at Kīlauea.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.hawaiian.pele' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《薄伽梵往世书》8.5 中，梵天带领受困的众神去见毗湿奴，随后才有乳海搅拌。 / In Bhāgavata Purāṇa 8.5 Brahmā leads the distressed gods to Viṣṇu before the churning of the ocean.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.hindu.brahma' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《第二次马格图雷德之战》中达格达之女布里格，为儿子鲁阿丹哀哭，是爱尔兰第一次听到的哀歌。 / Bríg, daughter of the Dagda in Cath Maige Tuired, whose keening for her son Rúadán is the first heard in Ireland.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.irish.bridig' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《第二次马格图雷德之战》中拥有“无人离去不饱足”之大锅的神；战前在乌恩辛河边与莫莉甘相会。 / In Cath Maige Tuired, owner of a cauldron from which no company left unsatisfied; meets the Morrígan at the Unshin before the battle.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.irish.dagda' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='“百艺之主”，在《第二次马格图雷德之战》中用投石击杀巴洛尔。 / The Samildánach, master of all arts, who in Cath Maige Tuired kills Balor with a sling stone.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.irish.lugh' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='恩玛斯之女；萨温节与达格达相会，许诺击杀因德赫，并在第二次马格图雷德之战后宣告胜利。 / Daughter of Ernmas who meets the Dagda at Samain, promises Indech''s death and proclaims the victory after the second battle of Mag Tuired.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.irish.morrigan' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《古事记》中的男性创世神：与伊邪那美造出淤能碁吕岛，追往黄泉，归来禊祓时生出天照大神、月读与须佐之男。 / Male creator deity of the Kojiki: with Izanami he forms Onogoro Island, follows her to Yomi, and on returning gives birth to Amaterasu, Tsukuyomi and Susanoo as he purifies himself.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.japanese.izanagi' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《古事记》中的女性创世神：与伊邪那岐一同造地，生火神后被灼伤而死，留在黄泉。 / Female creator deity of the Kojiki: with Izanagi she forms the land, dies after giving birth to the fire deity, and remains in Yomi.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.japanese.izanami' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='月神；《古事记》中伊邪那岐洗右眼时所生，张伯伦译作“掌管月夜者”。 / Moon deity born when Izanagi washes his right eye (Kojiki); Chamberlain renders the name ''Moon-Night-Possessor''.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.japanese.tsukuyomi' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='地母；与兰吉努伊相连，直到孩子们把他们分开（Te Ara 对共同线索的概述）。 / Earth mother joined to Ranginui until their children part them (Te Ara''s summary of common threads).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.maori.papatuanuku' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='天父；与帕帕图阿努库从黑暗中出现，孩子们把他们分开，光明由此进入世界（Te Ara）。 / Sky father who, with Papatūānuku, emerges from darkness; their children separate them and let in the light (Te Ara).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.maori.ranginui' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='玛雅雨神，古典期象形文字写作 Chahk；大都会博物馆的陶盘上他半身浸在水中。 / Maya rain god, written Chahk in Classic hieroglyphs; shown waist-deep in water on a Met plate.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.maya.chaac' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='年老的天神伊察姆纳（Itzamnaaj），有一个鸟形化身，在玛雅太初神话中地位重要（大都会博物馆，2022）。 / Aged celestial god Itzamnaaj with an avian avatar, important in Maya primordial myths (Met, 2022).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.maya.itzamna' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='与奇琴伊察“库库尔坎神庙”相连的羽蛇之名；联合国教科文组织称其为图拉统治者“羽蛇”名号的玛雅译名（通行说法）。 / Feathered-serpent name linked to El Castillo, the ''Temple of Kukulkan'' at Chichen-Itza; UNESCO reports it as the Maya rendering of a Tula ruler''s Quetzalcoatl name.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.maya.kukulkan' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='墨西加人的太阳战神与守护神；《佛罗伦萨手抄本》第三卷说他在蛇山全副武装地诞生；大神庙南侧是他的神殿。 / Solar war god and patron of the Mexica; born fully armed on Coatepec in Florentine Codex Book 3; his chapel stood on the south side of the Templo Mayor.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.mexica.huitzilopochtli' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《佛罗伦萨手抄本》第三卷中图拉的大法师，巫师们到来后他的荣光走向终结。 / Great wizard of Tollan whose glory ends when sorcerers come to him in Florentine Codex Book 3.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.mexica.quetzalcoatl' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='又称蒂特拉卡瓦；《佛罗伦萨手抄本》第三卷中令羽蛇神在图拉衰落的巫师之一。 / Also called Titlacauan; among the sorcerers who bring Quetzalcoatl''s glory at Tollan to an end (Florentine Codex Book 3).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.mexica.tezcatlipoca' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='与农业相关的雨神；大神庙北侧是他的神庙（墨西哥国家人类学与历史研究所）。 / Rain god linked to agriculture whose temple occupied the north side of the Templo Mayor (INAH).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.mexica.tlaloc' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='尼奥尔德之女；住在弗尔克范格，分得一半战死者，乘两只猫拉的车（《欺骗古鲁菲》第24章）。 / Daughter of Njörðr; lives at Fólkvangr, takes half the slain and drives a chariot drawn by two cats (Gylfaginning 24).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.norse.freyja' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='尼奥尔德之子，掌管雨水、阳光与丰收；为娶葛德而交出宝剑（《欺骗古鲁菲》第24、37章）。 / Son of Njörðr who rules rain, sunshine and the fruitfulness of the earth; gives away his sword to win Gerðr (Gylfaginning 24, 37).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.norse.freyr' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='奥丁之妻，知晓一切命运；她让万物发誓不伤害巴德尔，唯独漏掉了槲寄生（《欺骗古鲁菲》第20、49章）。 / Odin''s wife who knows all fates; she takes oaths from all things to protect Baldr, except the mistletoe (Gylfaginning 20, 49).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.norse.frigg' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='住在彩虹桥边希敏约格的众神守望者，掌管加拉尔号角（《欺骗古鲁菲》第27章）。 / Watchman of the gods at Himinbjörg by Bifröst, keeper of Gjallarhorn (Gylfaginning 27).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.norse.heimdall' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《欺骗古鲁菲》第23章中的华纳神：住在诺欧通，掌管风与海，是弗雷与芙蕾雅之父。 / Vanir god in Gylfaginning 23: lives at Nóatún, rules wind and sea, father of Freyr and Freyja.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.norse.njord' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='众神中最勇敢的一位；束缚芬里尔时失去一只手（《欺骗古鲁菲》第25、34章）。 / The boldest of the gods, who loses his hand when the wolf Fenrir is bound (Gylfaginning 25, 34).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.norse.tyr' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='Te Ara 所说的森林之神；在部分部族版本中是分开天地的重要角色。 / Named by Te Ara as atua of the forests; in some tribal versions important in separating earth and sky.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.polynesian.tane' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='Te Ara 所说的海洋之神，兰吉努伊与帕帕图阿努库的孩子之一。 / Named by Te Ara as atua of the sea, one of the children of Ranginui and Papatūānuku.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.polynesian.tangaroa' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《往年纪事》980 年条中弗拉基米尔在基辅山岗所立神像名单的最后一位；该处未说明其职能。 / Named last among the idols Volodimer set up on the Kyiv hill in the Primary Chronicle''s annal for 980; no function is stated there.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.slavic.mokosh' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='天上的老一辈神；《恩基与世界秩序》称恩基为“神圣的安所钟爱者”（ETCSL 1.1.3）。 / Senior god of heaven; Enki and the World Order praises Enki as beloved of holy An (ETCSL 1.1.3).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.sumerian.an' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='月神；带着礼物乘船前往父亲恩利尔的城市尼普尔，带回给乌尔的祝福（ETCSL 1.5.1）。 / Moon god who sails with gifts to Nibru, the city of his father Enlil, and returns with blessings for Urim (ETCSL 1.5.1).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.sumerian.nanna' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='恩基吃下迪尔蒙的植物后诅咒他、之后又生出众神为他治病的女神（ETCSL 1.1.1）。 / Goddess who curses Enki after he eats the plants of Dilmun and later brings forth deities to heal him (ETCSL 1.1.1).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.sumerian.ninhursag' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='太阳神；吉尔伽美什向他求助，他赐下勇士为远征胡瓦瓦引路（ETCSL 1.8.1.5）。 / Sun god whom Gilgameš asks for help; he grants warriors to guide the expedition against Ḫuwawa (ETCSL 1.8.1.5).',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.sumerian.utu' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='宾夕法尼亚大学博物馆对迦南众神的概述中，创造者伊勒的配偶阿西拉特（亚舍拉）。 / Athirat (Asherah), consort of El the creator in the Penn Museum''s overview of the Canaanite pantheon.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.ugaritic.asherah' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='活态约鲁巴神灵；在具名社区权威授权之前，本站不发布故事。 / Living Yorùbá orisha; no public story is published here until a named community authority grants scope.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.yoruba.ogun' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='活态约鲁巴传统中的至高存在；在具名社区权威授权之前，本站不发布故事。 / Supreme being in living Yorùbá tradition; no public story is published here until a named community authority grants scope.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.yoruba.olodumare' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='约鲁巴女神；联合国教科文组织记录把她与奥孙-奥索博神树林相连；活态信仰中的叙事需社区许可。 / Yoruba goddess whom UNESCO''s record links to the Osun-Osogbo Sacred Grove; living-practice narratives require community permission.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.yoruba.oshun' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《密赫尔颂》中的“广阔牧场之主”：阿胡拉·马兹达所造、与其同受崇拜，守护契约，有千耳万眼。 / Lord of wide pastures in the Mihr Yasht: created by Ahura Mazda as worthy of worship as himself, guardian of the contract, with a thousand ears and ten thousand eyes.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='deity.zoroastrian.mithra' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');
UPDATE entities SET description='《史记·五帝本纪》中少典之子轩辕，于涿鹿擒杀蚩尤并被尊为天子；本站不作历史真实性断言。 / Xuanyuan, son of Shaodian, who in the Shiji fights Chiyou at Zhuolu and is honoured as Son of Heaven; no historical-reality claim is made.',updated_at='2026-10-09T00:30:00Z' WHERE id='hero.chinese.yellow_emperor' AND (description IS NULL OR description='');

